            "name": "Inconsistent Interpretation of HTTP Requests ('HTTP Request/Response Smuggling')"
         },
         "notes": [
            {
               "category": "description",
               "text": "Gazelle versions through 0.49 for Perl allows HTTP Request Smuggling via Improper Header Precedence.\n\nGazelle incorrectly prioritizes \"Content-Length\" over \"Transfer-Encoding: chunked\" when both headers are present in an HTTP request. Per RFC 7230 3.3.3, Transfer-Encoding must take precedence.\n\nAn attacker could exploit this to smuggle malicious HTTP requests via a front-end reverse proxy.",
